    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d914">

                <pb facs="1393" n="1367" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg1367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/7–1454: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-07-14T12:00:00+01:00">July 14, 1954—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 603. Repeated information priority Paris 54. Limit distribution. Eyes only
                    Dillon and Johnson. Cheysson of French delegation told me this morning that when
                    Dong was given draft declaration (Secto 597<anchor n="1" xml:id="d914-f1"/>)
                    prepared by French delegate, his first reaction was to insist that the
                    conference should also take note of the fact that Democratic Republic of Vietnam
                    has stated its intention of examining the question of membership in the French
                    Union and of engaging in discussions with the French with a view to resuming
                    economic and cultural relations (Viet Minh May 10th proposals<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d914-f2"/>). French rejoined that this would hardly appear to be
                    suitable question for inclusion in final declaration designed to record some
                    measure of conference approval or acceptance of definite items. Cheysson added
                    that if Dong <pb facs="1394" n="1368" xml:id="pg1368"/> insists, some
                    satisfactory language of a general character might be found to cover this point,
                    “but of course we do not want them in the French Union”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bonsal</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d914-f1" n="1" xml:id="d914-f1-content">
                <p>Dated July 13, <ref target="#pg1355">p. 1355</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d914-f2" n="2" xml:id="d914-f2-content">
                <p>For the report of the Second Plenary Session on Indochina, May 10, see telegram
                    Secto 162, May 10, <ref target="#pg753">p. 753</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
